<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<p>This rule extends the base <a href="https://eslint.org/docs/rules/comma-dangle"><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">eslint/comma-dangle</code></a> rule.
It adds support for TypeScript syntax.</p>

<p>See the <a href="https://eslint.org/docs/rules/comma-dangle">ESLint documentation</a> for more details on the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">comma-dangle</code> rule.</p>

<h2 id="how-to-use">How to Use</h2>

<p>In addition to the options supported by the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">comma-dangle</code> rule in ESLint core, the rule adds the following options:</p>

<ul>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"enums"</code> is for trailing comma in enum. (e.g. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">enum Foo = {Bar,}</code>)</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"generics"</code> is for trailing comma in generic. (e.g. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">function foo&lt;T,&gt;() {}</code>)</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"tuples"</code> is for trailing comma in tuple. (e.g. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">type Foo = [string,]</code>)</li>
</ul>
